       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg add little blood pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nYou could do one of the following:\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 5 mg PO once daily**, a typical starting dose, and titrate up.\n3. **Add a second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if 10 mg isn't enough. I can enter that order too.\n4. **Enter 20 mg as written**, if you're intentionally exceeding the labeled maximum. Please confirm that, and I can add a note with your rationale.\n\nWhich would you like?"
